" :question/math-academy-id "q-78947" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x={t}^{3}-1,\\,y=3{t}^{6}+2$ where $t$ is a real number. Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=18{t}^{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{18{t}^{5}}{3{t}^{2}}=6{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(6{t}^{3})}{3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18{t}^{2}}{3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78947/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16dac5bd-acbd-51c6-8636-172e3a55aaf1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78947"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection/a500aa5ca3a335a17544c25b255481a5d3d4e4d0cf2c99ed89d2f436b72728fc" :answer/id #uuid "73a8eb8c-3607-56b4-9de7-d3f5b5292467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection/c2734755b254b9138ce68d558f29ba217ef2a3552a3d566d033f21e35a26375e" :answer/id #uuid "a90f1fc1-65bc-5b75-a002-a1c8cf7666ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}{csc}^{3}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection/503c2bb1c4db16493a63b6f7f0c97524202c88631bb4d91dc4723a4282dc72b2" :answer/id #uuid "02397ef0-344b-58b8-90bb-d83ca89137c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}{csc}^{2}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection/8de279f2adeb706675bdd0aadba6e3708021fa4377bfe4a84756ed0495916b14" :answer/id #uuid "687e5152-64e1-5f3c-9b5c-5fa8024ca85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{csc}^{3}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection/b8e9dc7dfcb80890bf366c50d47c1941d809dae7c8c14f000dc7d1f181190fe9" :answer/id #uuid "a9e0cad9-9d17-511c-9372-47170f23edaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{csc}^{3}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1788ef18-778e-5443-b559-964de5ac34c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122888/selection/c2734755b254b9138ce68d558f29ba217ef2a3552a3d566d033f21e35a26375e" :answer-field/choices ["q-122888/selection/a500aa5ca3a335a17544c25b255481a5d3d4e4d0cf2c99ed89d2f436b72728fc" "q-122888/selection/c2734755b254b9138ce68d558f29ba217ef2a3552a3d566d033f21e35a26375e" "q-122888/selection/503c2bb1c4db16493a63b6f7f0c97524202c88631bb4d91dc4723a4282dc72b2" "q-122888/selection/8de279f2adeb706675bdd0aadba6e3708021fa4377bfe4a84756ed0495916b14" "q-122888/selection/b8e9dc7dfcb80890bf366c50d47c1941d809dae7c8c14f000dc7d1f181190fe9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122888" :question/id #uuid "0600f53b-9fb9-50fc-9a9b-d28a258d380f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122888" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-10,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+15.$ Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=24\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{24\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)}=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4t).\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4t))}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12{csc}^{2}⁡(4t)}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{csc}^{3}⁡(4t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122888/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16dac5bd-acbd-51c6-8636-172e3a55aaf1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection/ba3ad363a0cf94b7f1585e3b2f6f07e3fb1083f0bdacada65e3790efbeeb502d" :answer/id #uuid "bf6c8872-d724-52b7-b08b-183e87133ffd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2+4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection/4cbd0f6bbebb3a8cfd5403e187d7bbdfd0054b0657975ea9f78476800ac44a52" :answer/id #uuid "8fa8c344-c348-5b10-a387-2139def3b16c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15{e}^{8t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection/26493c9b7c9886292e7ce03b7a1facaed5e21061896076ef603b89244737073f" :answer/id #uuid "4e925519-1db2-5bb5-a9c6-c508b906eb03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}{e}^{8-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection/58a8166c4c826990e6b953f475c718ec48eae3211e5f878779031c319c5af8be" :answer/id #uuid "c06ad589-eedd-5f6d-9209-413fe28f0204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{15}{e}^{-2-8t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection/215963c98b617fe7660b71a26dc6f25ef8793723f79c39ab41364779f03bb187" :answer/id #uuid "776acaeb-f992-5cea-bb78-00b08fd8b407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{2-8t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7bf77d-b817-5bde-beb0-e863897247b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122903/selection/58a8166c4c826990e6b953f475c718ec48eae3211e5f878779031c319c5af8be" :answer-field/choices ["q-122903/selection/ba3ad363a0cf94b7f1585e3b2f6f07e3fb1083f0bdacada65e3790efbeeb502d" "q-122903/selection/4cbd0f6bbebb3a8cfd5403e187d7bbdfd0054b0657975ea9f78476800ac44a52" "q-122903/selection/26493c9b7c9886292e7ce03b7a1facaed5e21061896076ef603b89244737073f" "q-122903/selection/58a8166c4c826990e6b953f475c718ec48eae3211e5f878779031c319c5af8be" "q-122903/selection/215963c98b617fe7660b71a26dc6f25ef8793723f79c39ab41364779f03bb187"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122903" :question/id #uuid "601fce0f-444c-5aa9-8cae-681efbedd5e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122903" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=3{e}^{5t+1},\\,y=5{e}^{2t}-7$ where $t$ is a real number. Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=15{e}^{1+5t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=10{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{10{e}^{2t}}{15{e}^{1+5t}}=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-1-3t}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-1-3t})}{15{e}^{1+5t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2{e}^{-1-3t}}{15{e}^{1+5t}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{15}{e}^{-2-8t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122903/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16dac5bd-acbd-51c6-8636-172e3a55aaf1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122903"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348295/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "858cb3db-5191-5d55-a47d-21207204175d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348295/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "2ccaa9ac-6693-54a9-8b45-1e346d481a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348295/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a358d85-f4d7-515d-9468-6665228a47f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348295/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer-field/choices ["q-348295/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-348295/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348295" :question/id #uuid "be541b4a-bb13-5d68-b1b5-d082754d05e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-348295" :question/problem "A curve has parametric equations $x={t}^{2}+1,\\,y={t}^{3}+4.$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}t,$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3}{2}t,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{2}+1)=2t\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{3}{2}t)}{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=\\frac{3}{4(2)}=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-348295/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb50541-88df-5f3f-b9e0-cf51edae401e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348295"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352390/field-1/35b3b93c2d60e1d8269a5ce9ebf59b1a5ba84102c64d9ab6c93ddedc26033dba" :answer/id #uuid "6f11ff6b-5cc9-55ab-a138-b73419ae3487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{80}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352390/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "94b4cd57-ce0f-52f0-a0f2-0292fcc15d3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352390/field-1/35b3b93c2d60e1d8269a5ce9ebf59b1a5ba84102c64d9ab6c93ddedc26033dba" :answer-field/choices ["q-352390/field-1/35b3b93c2d60e1d8269a5ce9ebf59b1a5ba84102c64d9ab6c93ddedc26033dba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352390" :question/id #uuid "84d2b5b2-de55-52a6-af4a-f2e1349bfd06" :question/math-academy-id "q-352390" :question/problem "A curve has parametric equations $x={t}^{5}+1,\\,y=\\frac{35}{6}{t}^{6}+2{t}^{5}+9.$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=7t+2,$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=7t+2,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{5}+1)=5{t}^{4}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(7t+2)}{5{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(7)}{5{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5{t}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=\\frac{7}{5({2}^{4})}=\\frac{7}{80}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352390/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb50541-88df-5f3f-b9e0-cf51edae401e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352390"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
